To be precise about the "Deep Learning" layer in between:
LLM training specifically uses deep learning — neural networks with many stacked layers (in this case, a "transformer" architecture) — which is why it sits one level deeper than general ML in the 
hierarchy. Not all machine learning is deep learning (e.g., a simple fraud-detection decision tree is ML but NOT deep learning), but all LLM training is both ML and deep learning.

Machine Learning (broad)
 ├── Classic ML (decision trees, regression, clustering — simpler, no neural networks)
 └── Deep Learning (neural networks with many layers)
       └── LLMs (Llama3, Claude, ChatGPT)

